  "observations": [
    "READDIR serializes only registered direct children in stable catalog order; opaque cookie is last catalog ID, not a filesystem descriptor",
    "Pagination reserves XDR list/EOF footer, bounds reply bytes, rejects invalid cookies and cannot-fit-first-entry requests",
    "UTF8 catalog names encode strictly to UTF16LE, including surrogate pairs, without accepting overlong UTF8",
    "Portmapper only reports configured NFSv2/mountv1 UDP endpoints; SET and other mutation procedures are unavailable",
    "Mount accepts known ASCII/UTF16LE export path and returns source-owned root handle; withdrawal removes export and refuses mount",
    "UMNT/UMNTALL are stateless peer acknowledgments and do not withdraw shared source",
    "Independent handwritten Python wire client exercises portmapper/export/mount/UMNT, Unicode READDIR/LOOKUP/GETATTR, full30001-byte READ and withdrawal"
  ],
